<!-- @opening -->
<p class="story-lead">A migration finished months ago. You remember the implementation details, but the review asks who benefited and which decisions you owned. Keep the evidence close to the work while it is easy to recover.</p>

<!-- @before The Brag Document :: staff -->
### Capture a result and its context

Record the baseline, what changed, the evidence after rollout and the people who contributed. Keep examples that map to your organization’s rubric. If an outcome is still unknown, record the measurement plan and follow up when you have the result. [Writing a brag document](https://jvns.ca/blog/brag-documents/).
